WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:00.893
- I love this.

00:00:00.893 --> 00:00:01.890
We just had Dolly on.

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:02.790
I love Dolly Parton,

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:04.309
and you recently sang for her, right?

00:00:04.309 --> 00:00:05.142
(audience applauds)
- Yeah.

00:00:05.142 --> 00:00:06.663
I love, isn't Dolly the best?

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:09.390
Yeah, I was really honored.
- Yeah.

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:12.450
- Lauren Sanchez and
Jeff Bezos had me come

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.250
and get to sing for her as she was awarded

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:17.490
that $100 million civility grant.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:18.720
It was incredible.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:20.197
And I actually got to sing
- Incredible.

00:00:20.197 --> 00:00:21.450
- "Jolene" for her there,

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:22.620
which made me very nervous,

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:24.350
but it was very fun. Yeah.

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:26.220
(audience claps and cheers)

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:27.053
- You know what?

00:00:27.053 --> 00:00:27.886
I'll tell you what.

00:00:27.886 --> 00:00:28.719
I've had to sing one

00:00:28.719 --> 00:00:30.060
of her songs in front of her

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.190
and it is terrifying,

00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:33.330
'cause you're, you know what I'm saying,

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:34.230
the person is there.

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:35.460
That's their baby.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:36.690
They made it iconic.

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:38.700
You're like, "What am I doing?"

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:39.870
It is terrifying.

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:42.090
Even if you feel like a confident singer,

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:45.360
it's like, "Man, don't
screw this up." (laughs)

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:46.830
- I had the sweat mustache,

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:47.663
the sweaty boobs,

00:00:47.663 --> 00:00:48.510
the whole nine yards.
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:50.610
You guys know what I'm talking about.

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:51.443
It's real.

00:00:51.443 --> 00:00:54.240
- I have the sweat trickles down the back.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:55.720
So that was real
- It's ugly. Yep.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:58.710
- So do you remember the
first time you met Dolly,

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:00.330
or maybe one of your favorite
experiences with her?

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:02.190
'cause you've worked with her a few times.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:04.590
- Yes. I grew up on a
homestead with an outhouse,

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:07.350
so her, for me growing up, was like a hero

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:09.570
because she had a somewhat
similar lifestyle.

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:12.120
So, I was really excited.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:13.860
I had her sing on a song of mine

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:15.420
called "My Father's Daughter."

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:16.500
She came in and sang.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:17.460
She showed up like that.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:19.363
That was 7:45 a.m.

00:01:19.363 --> 00:01:20.196
(audience laughs)

00:01:20.196 --> 00:01:22.680
She looks on point at all times.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:23.513
She put me at ease.

00:01:23.513 --> 00:01:25.020
She's like, "Now hey, I'm
so glad that I'm here,

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:26.220
but I need you to keep me honest

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:27.180
in case I don't sing good,

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:28.440
and in case you're too intimidated.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:29.700
I brought a guy to keep me honest."

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.819
And I was like, " Alright!"

00:01:31.819 --> 00:01:33.343
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:33.343 --> 00:01:34.176
It was amazing.

00:01:34.176 --> 00:01:35.133
- I love your impression.

